cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Planum, please cite it as below. Please also cite the data and
  atlases behind the views you use, and include the acknowledgements they
  require, both listed at
  https://planumatlas.com/docs/reference/references.html
type: software
title: Planum
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-11-22
abstract: >-
  Planum is an open 3D atlas of the human brain, where cortical and deep
  parcellations, tractography and the published findings for each region are
  read on the same anatomy. It is built from real MRI data, with the surface,
  the sections and the white-matter tracts all taken from the same brain, so
  they agree with one another. Widely used cortical parcellations and a
  histological atlas of the deep structures are drawn on that anatomy.
  Selecting a region brings up what has been reported about it in meta-
  analyses of the imaging literature, lesion studies, intracranial stimulation
  and large group comparisons, each with its source. A coordinate or a
  statistical map from a study can be placed on the brain to see where it
  falls, and a standard MNI template can be used as the anatomy instead.
authors:
